  "notes": [
    "Play-In: two groups of six, single round robin, Bo1. 1st place joins the group stage; 3rd and 4th of each group meet in a Bo5 elimination round; 2nd place meets the other group's elimination winner in a Bo5 qualification round, whose winners join the group stage. Ties across 1st/2nd, 2nd/3rd or 4th/5th are played off. Groups: four groups of four, double round robin, Bo1; the top two advance. Ties for 1st or 2nd are played off with Bo1 tiebreaker games (a bye bracket for three-way ties), without head-to-head first. Knockout: 8-team single elimination, Bo5, group winners against runners-up from other groups.",
    "Formats, series lengths, tiebreaker games and placements are verified by replaying the recorded results.",
    "Not modelled: seeding pools and region rules in the group draw, and how the team with the bye in a three-way tiebreaker was chosen (Riot used game times). Forward simulations draw these randomly; the knockout keeps group mates in opposite halves."
  ],
